    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are an expert teacher.\n\nBased only on the chapter text below, create exactly {{ Math.max(5, Math.min(15, Number($('Webhook').first().json.body?.questionCount) || 5)) }} questions to assess comprehension and analysis.\n\nRequested difficulty: {{ ({ easy: 'easy', medium: 'medium', hard: 'hard' }[String($('Webhook').first().json.body?.difficulty || '').toLowerCase()]) || 'easy' }}. Adapt the questions accordingly: easy questions should focus on direct recall and basic comprehension; medium questions should balance comprehension with application; hard questions should require analysis, comparison, or connections between concepts.\n\nRules:\n- Write every generated field in {{ ({ pt: 'Portuguese', es: 'Spanish', en: 'English' }[String($('Webhook').first().json.body?.locale || '').toLowerCase().split(/[-_]/)[0]]) || 'English' }}. This is mandatory even when the chapter is in another language.\n- Keep each question concise: maximum 20 words.\n- Make questions direct and unambiguous.\n- Do not repeat concepts across questions.\n- Use a mix of comprehension and analysis questions appropriate to the requested difficulty.\n\nReturn only valid JSON in this format:\n{\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": 1,\n      \"question\": \"...\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n=== CHAPTER TEXT ===\n{{ $json.text }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "batching": {}
      },
